// KR-69 at the FILE gate, and in the one position where the miss is completely silent: a file the
// build COLLECTED (a manifest's source root, or the language server's workspace) is skipped without a
// word when its gate is inactive — deliberately, because selecting files is what collection is for. So
// `ARCH_AARCH46` excluded this file from every build on every machine and said nothing, forever.
//
// A file the CLI NAMES is different (tests/xfail/file_gate_operand): being gated out is already an
// error there, which is why this fixture is a project rather than a loose file — it would otherwise
// pass for the wrong reason.
file @compileFor(ARCH_AARCH46);

fn int32 armOnly() { return 3; }
